      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={e}^{3x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{3x})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+{e}^{3x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =3{e}^{3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+{e}^{3x}\\cdot 4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{4} \\\\  & =3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}(3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
